  "prompt": "Is the family home deductible from the gross estate, and up to how much?",
  "runtimeCommit": "87ce0c7571f9bd57514b6c2dfb45e9427d19c6b6",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, the family home is deductible from the gross estate, up to a maximum of P10,000,000.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practical terms, this means that when calculating the estate tax, the value of the family home can be excluded from the total value of the estate, up to the specified limit. This deduction can significantly impact the overall estate tax due, making it essential for estate planning and administration. Executors and heirs should ensure that the family home is properly valued and documented to take full advantage of this deduction.",
